Hi, I'm trying to make JRI work, but i'm having a problem with the first 
step, Rengine constructor.
I call the method but it never returns, or it returns but does not 
continue with the code, returning no Exception at all, just it freezes! 
(prints the Start message but not the Finished one, nor the Error). 
Running in debug mode does not clarifies the problem.

This is my code:

import org.rosuda.JRI.Rengine;

public class Test {
    public static void main(String [] args)
        {
        System.out.println("Start")
        try{
            Rengine re = new Rengine(null, false, null);
        }catch(Exception e){System.out.println("Error");}

        System.out.println("Finished!");
        }
}

I'm on Windows XP, running  Eclipse 3.3, with R-2.7.1 and the latest 
rJava package; and jre 1.6.0_03.
I set the following environment variable in Eclipse:

R_HOME=C:\Program Files\R\R-2.7.1

And run java with -Djava.library.path="C:\Program 
Files\R\R-2.7.1\library\rJava\jri"


I 've tried also with different parameters of Rengine, sucha as 
"--no-save" or "--vanilla", with the same results. What am I doing 
wrong? Any ideas?

Thanks!
Rodrigo
